OL,3,GNEWSAResidents back keeping sustainable
OL,4,Aflower beds
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe majority of people in an East
OL,7,FSussex seaside town have backed
OL,8,Fpermanently replacing its former
OL,9,Fcolourful flowerbeds with a more
OL,10,Fsustainable design, according to a new
OL,11,Fsurvey.
OL,13,FIn 2025, businesses said they were
OL,14,F"disgusted" when Eastbourne Borough
OL,15,FCouncil (EBC) changed the traditional
OL,16,Flook of Carpet Gardens, a long-time
OL,17,Ftourist favourite, in a bid to reduce
OL,18,Fits carbon footprint.
OL,20,FSome even described the formative
OL,21,Fstages of the gravel-surfaced new
OL,22,Flay-out as akin to "a cat litter tray".
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,330,320,200,140,0,100
